    "lawCode": "Add §233-b, RP L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1944A\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the real property law, in relation to\ncampgrounds\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nProvides for the removal of disruptive guests from campgrounds.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAdds a new section, 233-b, to the real property law, which provides (1)\nfor the removal of disruptive guests from campgrounds by law enforcement\nofficials, (2) refunds of fees paid by guests removed from campgrounds,\nwhich is based upon the campground's daily rate, and (3) the removal of\nproperty belonging to evicted guests from campsites and the disposal of\nsuch property if unclaimed.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThere is no effective way to remove long-term (greater than one week)\ndisruptive guests from a campground. Under current law, it is necessary\nto commence eviction proceedings against such guests, which can take a\nmatter of weeks, if not months. In the meantime, these guests often\nrepeat their disruptive behavior, which prevents other guests from\nenjoying their camping experiences. This bill provides for the removal\nof disruptive guests who repeat their disruptive behavior by a law\nenforcement officer, who may cite them with trespass.  It also provides\nthese guests with a fair refund of their prepaid camping fees and a\nmeans to reclaim their property and to dispose of property that is left\nbehind.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018: Died in Judiciary committees of both houses\n2015-16: Passed in Senate; died in Assembly Judiciary\n2013-14: Passed in Senate; Died in Assembly Judiciary\n2011-12: Passed in Senate; Died in Assembly Judiciary\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
